The WinExam directory contains 25 example programs (exam01 through
exam25) that serve as both a quick start and a tutorial for the
Windows Development System.

On Linux/macOS (with Wine), each example directory already contains a
GNU makefile.  Build individual examples with:

    make

On Windows (NMAKE), the example directories do not ship with NMAKE
makefiles installed.  You must first run the WINDOWS batch file from
the WinExam\setup directory to copy the necessary makefile.msc and
icon files into each example directory:

    cd WinExam\setup
    windows

Then build individual examples with:

    cd WinExam\exam10
    nmake -f makefile.msc

The following batch files are available in the WinExam\setup directory:

WINDOWS
Copies makefile.msc and algocorp.ico into all example directories.
Must be run before building examples with NMAKE.

CLEANALL
Deletes all files produced by builds in all example directories.

REALCLN
Deletes all build products and configuration files from all example
directories (returns to an as-shipped state).

CLEAN
Deletes all files produced by a build for a single example.
Run from the particular example's directory.
